# Mission A, FAST arm: the same pipeline at 2 m/s instead of 0.25 m/s.
#
# WHY A SEPARATE FILE: `phase_a_mission.parm` is the precision configuration the 10-flight table in
# docs/metrics/stepB-rectangle-20261013.txt was measured with, and its numbers must stay comparable to
# what it flew.  This file is the other arm -- user's request, 2026-10-14: "WP_SPD 0.25 m/s 慢速飞太慢了，
# 搞2m/s飞行行不行".
#
# THE GEOMETRY HAS TO CARRY THE SPEED, or the number is a lie.  Reaching v and braking from it costs
# v^2/(2*a) at each end of every leg:
#     2.0 m/s with WP_ACC 2.5  -> 0.80 m to accelerate + 0.80 m to brake = 1.60 m of every leg
# so the 2.0 x 1.2 m square of `worlds/pillars.yaml` (legs of 2.0 and 1.2 m) can never hold 2 m/s: it
# would peak near 1.1 m/s on the long legs and never reach the short ones.  That is why this arm flies
# `worlds/pillars_fast.yaml`: a 6.0 x 4.0 m square in an 18 x 18 m arena whose pillar clearance to the
# square is 2.20 m -- comfortably more than the 0.80 m braking distance.  (The old world's clearance is
# 0.60 m, i.e. at 2 m/s the vehicle could not stop before a pillar, and SITL has no obstacle collision,
# so that combination would have produced numbers that look fine and mean nothing.)
#
# The vertical is unchanged: the altitude loop is the LIO's (EK3_SRC1_POSZ = 6) and the take-off/landing
# profile is the same.
WP_SPD 2.0
LOIT_SPEED_MS 2.0
WP_RADIUS_M 0.10
WP_ACC 2.5
WP_JERK 2.0
LOIT_ACC_MAX_M 3.0
LOIT_BRK_ACC_M 3.0
LOIT_BRK_JRK_M 3.0
PSC_ACCZ_P 0.5
